e thin. Cut out circles of 12cm either with a cookie cutter or with a smaller plate/dish. Put two to three teaspoons of the dulce de leche in the middle of each circle. Brush the edges with milk, I do this with my pinkie. Fold each circle in half so that you have a half moon and press down the edges with a fork. You can also turn the edges about half a centimeter inwards every centimeter or so to create a pattern. Incorporate 8.3 tbsp butter, 1 whole egg, 3 tbsp milk, 1.1 oz butter, 1.1 oz sugar, and 1 tsp cinnamon smoothly until evenly distributed."}]]}],["$","li","3",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Bake Chocolate empanadas & Check Doneness"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Bake for 30 minutes until the edges turn golden and set while the center remains tender. Test with a toothpick—if it comes out with a few moist crumbs rather than wet batter, it is ready."}]]}],["$","li","4",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Cream Butter & Sugar Fluffy"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Place the prepared empanadas on the baking sheet and brush with egg wash. Bake for about 20-25min. Towards the end of the baking time, melt the remaining butter and mix the sugar and cinnamon in a small bowl. Once you take the empanadas out, immediately brush with the butter and sprinkle with the sugar mix. Empanadas can be enjoyed either still warm or cold. If eating warm, be careful not to burn yourself with hot filling!"}]]}]]}],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","dubai-brownies",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/dubai-pistachio-brownies/","children":"Giant Stuffed Dubai Pistachio & Kataifi Brownies"}]}],["$","li","nutella-lava-skillet",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/molten-nutella-lava-cookie-skillet/","children":"Molten Nutella Lava Cookie Skillet"}]}],"$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16"]}]]}]}]
